  "measurement_method": [
    "Three interleaved rounds; each case settles for 35 frames and samples 90 uncapped, vsync-disabled frames.",
    "Normal Mirror is 1280x720 with 2x MSAA. RT is 640x360, with primary and sun/local shadow rays.",
    "Mirror pass timing uses engine viewport measurements; RT GPU timestamps bracket queued reflection work.",
    "CPU bracket at process priorities 99-101 measures reflection-controller work. It excludes ordinary game work and the later render-thread CPU work.",
    "The matched half-size Mirror diagnostic freezes its controller after setting size once; only use its GPU pass for comparison.",
    "The moving benchmark animates and translates one real character every frame in both modes; other units remain hidden.",
    "Aggregate FPS is the reciprocal of the median of the three round-median wall times."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Shared development machine with concurrent work; frame rates are not isolated performance qualification.",
    "RT has different pixels, AA, shaders and shadow coverage from Mirror. GPU cost does not establish an equal-quality or whole-frame speedup.",
    "One selected water level, one reflection bounce and hard direct-light shadows; no global illumination, denoising or recursive reflections.",
    "Particles, shader-only wind/procedural deformation, blended transparency and in-place texture/mesh edits are omitted.",
    "Camera-specific body shaders are approximated; first-person body/crowded combat performance is not qualified by these fixtures.",
    "Caps: 320000 unique triangles, 4096 instances, 192 mipmapped 512x512 texture layers; extra CPU/GPU memory and rebuild hitches remain.",
